return {
    ["        夏尔，算算时间他应该已经去世了。死亡是一份礼物，希望他能作为普通人去度过幸福的一生。这是我们其他所有人都无法获得的平静……\n        博诺瓦……该死的蒸汽与机械之神，别让我逮到你！还有查拉图和“门”，等我复活了，我绝对一个个上门好好拜访！我的孩子应当肆意自由地活着，而不是成为神明的傀儡！不知道他那纯粹的神性中，有没有那么一点对我这个父亲的爱……一点点就够了。\n        心爱的贝尔纳黛，应验了查拉图的预言，她终究憎恨、厌弃和离开了我。不知道我被刺杀后她怎么样了……\n        头开始疼了，那家伙的呓语声真是难听。我又得睡了，我不会将这份污染带到这个世界上，这里还有我想守护的东西。哈哈，就跟我一起被封印在这里吧！\n        但我终会归来，只要我的子民还在信仰我，只要我留下的文明与规则没有消逝，只要这个世界还有人记得我的名字……连归来的口号我都想好了——因蒂斯的子民们，你们的皇帝回来了！\n        但在又一次的沉眠前，我似乎看到了一些被我遗忘了许久的东西……炸鸡、可乐、游戏机、家，和好像老去了一些的爸妈……\n        那是或许平凡乏味但再也回不去的人生。\n        故乡啊……"] = "        Charles, calculating the time, he should have passed away by now. Death is a gift; I hope he can spend a happy life as an ordinary person. This is a peace that none of the rest of us can ever obtain...\n        Bernadette... damn you, God of Steam and Machinery, don't let me catch you! And Zarathul and the \"Door,\" once I am resurrected, I will definitely visit you one by one! My child should live freely and wantonly, not become a puppet of the gods! I wonder if there is even a tiny bit of love for me, her father, in that pure divinity of hers... just a little bit would be enough.\n        My beloved Bernadette, Zarathul's prophecy has come true; she eventually hated, abandoned, and left me. I wonder how she is doing after I was assassinated...\n        My head is starting to ache; that guy's babbling is truly unpleasant. I have to sleep again. I will not bring this corruption into this world; there are still things here I want to protect. Haha, just be sealed here with me!\n        But I will eventually return, as long as my people still believe in me, as long as the civilization and rules I left behind have not faded, as long as there is still someone in this world who remembers my name... I have even thought of the slogan for my return—People of Intis, your Emperor has returned!\n        But before falling into another slumber, I seem to have seen some things I had forgotten for a long time... fried chicken, cola, game consoles, home, and my parents who seem to have aged a bit...\n        That is a life that might have been ordinary and dull, but one I can never return to.\n        My homeland...",
